#setp [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-00-invert 1

net	  relay_4KA1 [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-07
net	  relay_4KA59 [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-08
net	  relay_4KA58 [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-09
net	  relay_2KAM [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-10
net	  relay_2KAA [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-11
net	  relay_UNUSED_01 [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-13

net   x-servopack-fault [HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).input-02

#		x-enable relay is relay-2KAX 
net	  	x-enable			[HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-04
#		y-enable-relay is relay-2KAY 
net	  	y-enable 			[HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-05
#	  	z-enable-relay is relay-2KAZ 
net	  	z-enable			[HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-06
#		relay-2KAZ1 is Z Brake
net   	z-brake-release		[HMOT](CARD0).[HMOT](CARD1).output-12


##MORBIDELLI SPINDLE FAULT CHAIN: (SUPERSEDED BY MODBUS)
##power to VFD is supplied by BREAKER 4QF15 which is monitored by wire blue 25 to blue 514. 25 goes to VFD relay FAULT terminal 30C (relay common, NC to term. 30B). (30A isn't connected). 30B is wire 80, system +24VDC supply. 514 suspected signal to PR2 Input. Logic: if breaker broken, or if vfd is faulted, this line goes low. 
##additional safety: 511 VFD terminal P1 to BREAKER 5QFFR IN, OUT is 517 to BRAKING RESISTOR IN, OUT is 512 to DC brake terminal -. Breaker sensor is 500 NC to 506; if Braking resistor overcurrents, breaker trips, 506 to THERM input on VFD trips and VFD faults out.  


